# The machine's own cron, as the Hermes (gateway) user. Not hermes cron: that
# clock lives inside the gateway and stops with it.
#
# Assumes the checkout at /opt/hermes-watchdog and the floor fetched once with
#   /opt/hermes-watchdog/floor/fetch-floor.sh
#
# quick-check.sh's defaults assume the Hermes user is "hermes"; set HERMES_USER,
# HERMES_HOME and HERMES_BIN if yours differs (see the header of the fetched file).

# The agent jobs (2 and 3) run through agent-cage: their own cage, at most one CPU
# core, and ended together with everything they started at --max, even when
# nobody waits for them any more. On 2026-09-21 an agent's command outlived its
# caller and held a CPU core for 5.4 days until the host throttled the server.
# agent-cage comes from kit-bootstrap; install it once, as root:
#   curl -fsSLO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MichaelZelbel/kit-bootstrap/agent-cage-v1.0.2/agent-cage.sh
#   sha256sum agent-cage.sh   # 8b995b52a76220c94d9d8f25e9a406a0164e06c0a4da6cd0afd048353379bc9e
#   bash agent-cage.sh install && bash agent-cage.sh selftest
# Without it, drop the "/usr/local/bin/agent-cage --max ... --" in front of each
# job: selftest.sh and run-prompt.sh still bound their Hermes call with timeout,
# and they use agent-cage by themselves whenever it is installed. The floor
# (job 1) is plain shell and stays outside the cage.
# Run from a normal user's crontab, agent-cage cannot join the system cage and
# falls back to timeout plus nice: the time limit still holds for the whole job.

PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
HERMES_USER=hermes

# 1. the floor: is the gateway alive? restart once if not
*/5 * * * *  /opt/hermes-watchdog/floor/quick-check.sh
# 2. the self-check: can the watchdog Hermes answer one word?
*/5 * * * *  /usr/local/bin/agent-cage --max 10m -- /opt/hermes-watchdog/templates/selftest.sh
# 3. the operator: diagnose, repair within bounds, report
7 * * * *    /usr/local/bin/agent-cage --max 30m -- /opt/hermes-watchdog/templates/run-prompt.sh hourly-quick-repair
23 */6 * * * /usr/local/bin/agent-cage --max 30m -- /opt/hermes-watchdog/templates/run-prompt.sh six-hour-deep-check
# weekly update check, only if the operator has approved automatic updates
# 41 4 * * 1  /usr/local/bin/agent-cage --max 30m -- /opt/hermes-watchdog/templates/run-prompt.sh update-maintenance
